The first thing either program does is read this directory. Nothing here is
compiled in; everything here is a knob you can turn before the window opens.

Nothing runs yet -- phase 1 has not been built -- so this file describes what the
programs will look for rather than what they currently read.

--

## Both programs

  painting          which file in assets/ is the board.
                    default: vision-map.png

  network           which fence network to load.
                    default: assets/fences  (does not exist yet)

  window            width and height. The tome takes a fixed slice of the width
                    and the map gets the rest.
                    default: 1600 x 900

  tome-width        how wide the written half is, in pixels.
                    default: 420

## The game

  zoom-floor        the most zoomed-out the view may go. Below "fit the pane"
                    there is nothing to see but letterbox.
                    default: fit the pane

  zoom-ceiling      the most zoomed-in. Past native pixels the painting is being
                    magnified rather than revealed.
                    default: 1.0

  fence-fade        the two on-screen block widths between which a fence ramps
                    from invisible to solid.
                    default: 24 and 64

  glow-period       how long one breath takes, in seconds.
                    default: 2.5

  glow-floor        the opacity a glow never falls below.
                    default: 0.3

  filters           which filters start active, and for each one its colour, its
                    hatch angle, and its stacking mode.

  theme             how the text pane is styled. The prototype's black ground
                    with coloured words is a starting point, not the design.

## The tracing tool

  snap-radius       the grab distance for adopting a vertex or an edge, measured
                    in screen pixels rather than painting pixels, because it
                    should match how precisely a hand can point right now.
                    default: 8

  trace-floor       the zoom below which placing and dragging vertices is
                    refused, so that imprecise work is never silently accepted.

  autosave          how often the network is written to tmp/shared-memory/,
                    because losing an hour of tracing is the worst thing that
                    could happen to this project.
